.TH "PB-CONFIG-TEAM-DEFAULT-UNADOPT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-team-default-unadopt - Stop inheriting a team configuration default


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config team-default-unadopt [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop inheriting a team configuration default

.PP
Stop this account inheriting its adopted team repository default. Personal machine assignments, the team's default, and other members' choices remain unchanged.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for team-default-unadopt

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config(1)\fP
